  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-61684",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "Interpreting the fractions as division, we get\n\n$$\n(15\\,÷\\,4)\\times (16\\,÷\\,3).\n$$\n\n \n\nSince our expression contains multiplication and division only, we can create an equivalent expression by swapping the $÷\\,4$ and $÷\\,3$:\n\n \n\n$$\n(15\\,÷\\,3)\\times (16\\,÷\\,4)\n$$\n\n \n\nInterpreting the divisions as fractions, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{15}{3}\\times \\frac{16}{4}.\n$$\n\nCarrying out the divisions, we arrive at\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{{\\frac{15}{3}}_{⏟}}_{5}\\times {{\\frac{16}{4}}_{⏟}}_{4}=5\\times 4=20.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
